WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:06.625 line:0 align:center
You can add any Android app from your phone to a button on the dash.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.250 line:0 align:center
The app opens in the large main area of the dash, usually where the map is.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.475 line:0 align:center
To show an app full screen, put it in its own sub dash.

00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:25.175 line:0 align:center
Then open that sub dash with a button.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.975 line:0 align:center
These sub dashes all open full screen.

00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:33.725 line:0 align:center
The main area can be resized, as big as you like.

00:00:34.975 --> 00:00:39.300 line:0 align:center
For the best experience, keep full-screen apps in their own sub dash.

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:46.450 line:0 align:center
Two widgets take the main space of the dash: App and Camera.

00:00:47.225 --> 00:00:51.400 line:0 align:center
App shows an Android app from your phone, right inside the dash.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.875 line:0 align:center
Camera shows the camera you selected in the MOTO-HUB Dashcam module.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:00.600 line:0 align:center
It shows one camera at a time.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.075 line:0 align:center
It can be any camera the module supports, not only a bike dash cam.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.200 line:0 align:center
For example, an IP camera at home.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:18.050 line:0 align:center
Dash works on any screen that supports Android Auto, and replaces Android Auto there.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.400 line:0 align:center
Have fun, and see you on Discord.
